.TH ciaaw 1 "07 October 2026" "1.3.3" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
\"{{{
ciaaw \- CLI for ciaaw
\"}}}

.SH SYNOPSIS
\"{{{
.B ciaaw
[\fIOPTION\fP]\.\.\. [\fIELEMENT\fP]\.\.\.
\"}}}

.SH DESCRIPTION
\"{{{
.B ciaaw 
is a command line interface which provides the atomic
weights, the isotopic compositions and the nuclides atomic weights.
If no element is provided the full periodic table is displayed.
\"}}}

.SH OPTIONS
\"{{{
.TP
.B
\-s, \-\-saw 
Get the standard atomic weight.
.TP
.B
\-i, \-\-ice 
Get the isotopic composition.
.TP
.B
\-n, \-\-naw 
Get the nuclide atomic weight.
.TP
.B
\-m, \-\-mu 
Get the molar masses in g/mol by multiplying the
atomic weights by the molar mass constant Mu.
.TP
.B
\-c, \-\-colnames
Show the headers in the outputs.
.TP 
.B
\-M, \-\-molarmass SPECIES
Compute the molar mass of the given species.
.TP
.B
\-u, \-\-usage
Show usage text and exit.
.TP
.B
\-v,\-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.B
\-h, \-\-help
Show help text and exit.
\"}}}

.SH EXAMPLE
\"{{{
Minimal example
.nf
.ft CR
      ciaaw
      ciaaw H C B O Zr Nb --saw --ice --naw --colnames
      ciaaw H C B O Zr Nb -sinc
.ft R
.fi
\"}}}
